EOSmith -> Middletown[label="18.5
05/07", weight="82", tooltip="NEIRA Boys & Girls Fours,Middletown High School, E.O. Smith, Valley Regional			
Distance: 1500 Meters Conditions: Float starts on the Connecticut River. Current was almost non existent, due to the current going out while the tide came in. Ten mph tail wind with moderate chop & occasional 20 mph gusts. Race course requires a slight turn to port at approximately the 750 meter mark. Comments: MHS Boys 1V 3 seat jumped a slide approximately 1200 meters into the race & had to stop rowing until the athlete returned to their seat.
Valley Regional Boys 2V incurred a 10 second penalty for cutting the turn to port too early, shortening the course by going on the wrong side of the buoy. Original time was 5:38.95.
Girls 2V Race included Middletown B Boat (Their 3V boat in a 2V race) that came in 2nd.
Note for CPSRA: 4th boats are novice races. We also did a mixed novice 8. Times below:
EO Smith: 6:22.34
MHS 6:43.53 - 4 seat caught two craps causing all rowers to stop both times.
